"""
Rework the reset behavior to fully rely on software reset. 
The dtr method is just too unreliable in the long run.
Remove the reset system from the transport layer 
and move it to the firmware command handler. 
This way, the host can send a reset command to the device, 
and the device will respond with an acknowledgment before performing the reset. 
This should be more reliable and avoid issues with USB CDC re-enumeration on the host side.
The reset function need to use _await_device_ready() 
"""